# Generated from analysis/generated/symbols.json for pinned MesenCE.
# Native syntax: MemoryType:HEX_ADDRESS:Label[:Comment].
SnesPrgRom:0C41:Text_TestCharacterMetadataBit7:Shared helper reached from four text/layout loops including `03:8998`, `00:C4CB`, and `00:C510`. It indexes the byte table at `00:C6F8` by character code and tests bit 7. Printable-table inspection shows uppercase A-Z in the low half while lowercase a-z, digits and much punctuation usually carry bit 7; therefore this is a verified character-metadata class test, not yet a proven glyph-width flag.
SnesPrgRom:B8F1:RNC1_Unpack:Identified by unique opcode-structure match to preserved 1992 SNES `RNC_1.S`; ROM offset `0x00B8F1`. Regional/build equivalents: Europe retail `01:B8E2` (`0x00B8E2`), 1994-11-29 PAL prototype `01:B8D1` (`0x00B8D1`), legacy beta identical to USA.
SnesPrgRom:BB60:RNC1_MakeHuffTail:Preserved Method-1 MAKEHUFF tail begins here; final RTS at `01:BB6E`, establishing the shipped generic RNC1 body end.
SnesPrgRom:BB6F:RNC1_ReadWordLoROMSafe:Integration helper used by the shipped Method-1 decoder for a 16-bit packed-stream read through `IN`. Normal path returns `LDA [IN]` while restoring the pointer; when `IN=$FFFF`, it fetches the high byte from next-bank `$8000`, matching LoROM linear-stream continuity across a bank boundary. `01:BB73` is the helper's wrap-test `BNE`, not a store.
SnesPrgRom:1007E:APU_UploadBlockById_Wrapper:Exact bytes `JSR $8082; RTL`. Callers load X with audio block IDs before entering; the body at `02:8082` performs the SPC handshake and calls `APU_ResolveBlockPointer` at `02:812A`, establishing X as a block-record selector.
SnesPrgRom:1012A:APU_ResolveBlockPointer:Exact static routine maps block ID X onto the packed audio-record pool beginning at `10:8000`. It walks X length-prefixed records, performing LoROM bank-wrap arithmetic, and returns the selected record pointer in DP `$63-$65`. The 50 valid selector IDs `$00-$31` therefore address 50 consecutive records.
SnesPrgRom:18971:Text_HandleFCPositionControl:Bounded static analysis of the Sayans translation-control grammar. The routine preserves A, recognizes low-byte `FC`, consumes the following parameter, scans subsequent character bytes until `FF` or `FB`, consults `Text_TestCharacterMetadataBit7` for ordinary bytes, then computes `parameter * 32 + horizontal adjustment` into DP `$9F`. The 32-column arithmetic and translated `FF FC xx` / `FB FC xx` sequences support a centered tilemap-position/layout role. Exact user-facing meaning of the parameter remains unpromoted.
SnesWorkRam:000E:Frontend_SelectedRow:Recovered bot label; native route captures row `0x00` through the verified clean frontend route. Exact semantics outside these menus not yet tested.
SnesWorkRam:009B:Frontend_SelectedOption:Recovered bot uses it for main-menu/tour selection. Native captures show `0x00` at clean main menu and first tours page, consistent with bot policy.
SnesWorkRam:009F:Frontend_CurrentMenu:Verified in both native and Snes9x/snesref deterministic runs: `0xD7` main menu, `0x3C` one-player rider select, `0x6D` first one-player tours page, `0xF6` one-player track select, `0x16` now-playing screen, then `0x00` after race entry.
SnesWorkRam:0313:Race_ActiveState:Recovered bot label `inRace`; verified as `0x01` after deterministic race entry in both native and Snes9x/snesref runs. Non-race screens can contain other transient values, so only `0x01 = active race` is currently asserted.
SnesWorkRam:0411:Player1_XPosition:Effective recovered-bot word key `xPos`. Race-acceleration run 36512546762 moves it identically in native/reference from 1088 at rest to 1655 under staged Right input, alongside positive X speed.
SnesWorkRam:0415:Player1_YPosition:Effective recovered-bot word key `yPos`. Sustained-B run 36514981164 causally changes player 1 from ground Y=859 in the matched no-B control to Y=797 while airborne; native and Snes9x match exactly.
SnesWorkRam:042B:Player1_ZFlipCount:Recovered USJO v8 reads this byte as the completed Z-flip counter; independently present in the historical TAS watch list.
SnesWorkRam:042F:Player1_TabletopCount:Recovered USJO v8 reads this byte as the completed tabletop counter; independently present in the historical TAS watch list.
SnesWorkRam:04B7:Player1_XSpeed:Effective recovered-bot word key `xSpeed`; bot explicitly sign-converts it. Race-acceleration run 36512546762 changes it identically from 0 to +447 under Right input while X position increases.
SnesWorkRam:04BB:Player1_YSpeed:Effective recovered-bot word key `ySpeed`; bot sign-converts it. In run 36514981164 sustained B changes it causally from 0 in the matched control to -21 while player 1 is airborne; native and Snes9x match exactly.
SnesWorkRam:04C7:Player1_PitchAngle:Persistent player-1 pitch/orientation. From control angle `0x07`, eight L frames produce `0x37` (= 7−16 mod 64) and eight R frames produce `0x17` (= 7+16 mod 64), identically native/reference. ROM `02:8D84` copies working `$0F49` into this slot.
SnesWorkRam:04C9:Player2_PitchAngle:Paired player-2 pitch/orientation slot. Sibling ROM routine at `02:9272` executes `LDY $0F49; STY $04C9`; surrounding destinations shift coherently to player-2 fields.
SnesWorkRam:0545:Player1_AirState:Effective player-1 Lua key `airValue`; later duplicate overrides second-racer `7E:0547`. In run 36514981164 sustained B causally changes player 1 from 0 to 9 while Y position/speed enter the airborne trajectory; matched no-B control remains 0.
SnesWorkRam:0BA1:Player1_FacedDirection:Recovered bot: 1 = right, 0 = left. Not yet independently validated.
SnesWorkRam:0C63:Frontend_SelectedColumn:Recovered bot label; native captures change with frontend scene/selection. Rider-select ready state captures `0x06`, matching the bot's left-column target value.
SnesWorkRam:0DFD:Player1_ZRotationState:USJO v8 working label `zrotation`; used to gate Z-flip timing. Exact physical meaning not yet locally reproduced.
SnesWorkRam:0F49:CurrentPlayer_PitchScratch:Historical bot reads this as `pitch`, but static sibling routines copy the same working value into persistent player-1 `$04C7` or player-2 `$04C9` slots. L-vs-control checkpoints leave `$0F49` unchanged while `$04C7` changes causally, so it should not be treated as stable player-1 storage.
SnesWorkRam:0F57:Player1_ZPreRotationState:USJO v8 working label `zprerotation`; consulted during chained Z-flip timing. Exact meaning not yet locally reproduced.
SnesWorkRam:0F61:Player1_TwistCount:Recovered USJO v8 reads this byte as the completed twist counter; the 2008 TAS watch list independently labels it “# of Twists.” Local transition semantics still need reproduction.
SnesWorkRam:0F9F:Player1_XSpeed_Alternate:USJO v8 comment names this as an alternative to `7E:04B7` for horizontal speed. Treat as a lead until reader/writer relationship is understood.
SnesWorkRam:0FCB:Player1_ArrowDirection:Effective duplicate-key address used by recovered bot; 0 = right, 1 = left.
SnesWorkRam:0FCC:Player1_ArrowsVisible:Effective duplicate-key address used by recovered bot; 0 means direction arrows showing.
SnesWorkRam:11BA:Race_CountdownTimer:Recovered bot word key shared by players. In run 36512546762 it decreases identically in native/reference by exactly `0x0100` per guest frame across the staged pre-start/acceleration checkpoints. Exact game-facing units/threshold meanings remain to be named.
SnesWorkRam:11CD:Player1_BoostMeter:Historical TAS watch list labels a 16-bit unsigned booster meter; USJO v8 reads only the low byte as `realboostmeter` and uses zero/nonzero gating. Verify width/units before stronger promotion.
SnesWorkRam:11F9:Player1_RollCount:Recovered USJO v8 reads this byte as the completed roll counter; independently present in the historical TAS watch list.
SnesWorkRam:11FD:Player1_FlipCount:Recovered USJO v8 reads this byte as the completed flip counter; independently present in the historical TAS watch list.
SnesWorkRam:132B:Race_ReverseControls:Recovered bot: 2 = controls reversed, 0 = normal. Not yet independently validated.
SnesWorkRam:1509:Camera_ScreenXPosition:Historical TAS watch list labels this “Screen X Position.” Not consumed by v8; local camera/unit semantics still need validation.
SnesWorkRam:10000:Course_ActiveDecodedPayload:Confirmed by run 36514985916: active Dragster decoded stream 1 matches 33,814/33,815 bytes from this address; only decoded byte 11 is runtime-mutated.
